  "guide": {
   "buffPoints": [
    "**Price what a card offers, never who receives it.** A buff is priced for what it gives, not for the card that ends up with it.",
    "**Price against maximums, never live state.** Pips mean maximum capacity.",
    "**Don't price a keyword off another stat on the same card.** Rare synergies are unpriced upside; Mult reading attack and charge-fed effects reading pips are the exceptions.",
    "**Effects on a card that dies early** (self-healing, Taunt, Guard) are priced low."
   ],
   "findings": [
    "**The 6/12 shape.** Mirror matches, 6v6 and 8v8 exterior rows, with and without a Shields (22) and Armor (25) pair, hull 20, the old Maelstrom (from round 12, 1 more to each hull a round): 6 attack, 12 health is the only shape that stays in or near 6 to 8 rounds in every configuration. Leaning to health runs into the Maelstrom; leaning to attack ends in about two rounds.",
    "**Fight length (2026-10-08).** Full 8×8 boards with 5 guns each and the Maelstrom from round 10 (hitting cards): the example boards' fights end in 6 to 10 rounds. With 3 guns in 6 exterior slots and the old Maelstrom they ran 11 to 12: the fight was decided by about round 5 and the rest was mop-up.",
    "Damage matters most early, so weapons belong behind the Armor.",
    "The first mover wins about 55% of even fights.",
    "Boarding is about numbers: equal crews stall, and boarding pays off against a thin interior.",
    "Pierce looked worthless only because the sims had empty interior rows.",
    "To re-check: fight length with plain Shields at {shields} and Armor at {armor}."
   ],
   "handPrices": [],
   "notes": {
    "Activate": "Provisional: re-measure",
    "Ammo": "Price per attack point: 8 × ammo ÷ (7 × reclaim), reclaim 30% + 70% × (ammo − 1) ÷ 6. 3.8 a point at 1 ammo, full price from 7. Baseline: a 6-attack Cannon deals 42 over 7 volleys",
    "Attack": "The first hit. 6 attack and 12 health (2:1) is the only shape that kept mirror fights in or near 6 to 8 rounds in every sim configuration",
    "AttackPerWin": "Priced by break-even: base stats break even after about 1.5 cycles and the card pays back around cycle 3. On Death triggers balance themselves",
    "Block": "A count; never scales with mark. Cheaper than Resist, since it is weak against mult. Revisit if it shuts down big single hits",
    "ChargeBlock": "The 1.5 is a refill premium, since charges can come back mid-fight. Only 1 pip is realistic at Mk I",
    "ChargeReflect": "Pip surcharge 0, 8, 20, 36, 56, 80 for 1 to 6 pips; never more than always-on Reflect",
    "Discharge": "Spreads onward instead of wasting, so it sits on the top tier",
    "DoubleDamage": "Provisional: re-measure",
    "Execute": "Six attack points' worth: it nearly always secures kills. Nudge toward 64 if it proves oppressive",
    "Flank": "Four attack points' worth: it reaches the glass cannons behind the tanks",
    "FreeRestore": "Every Shields card has Restore equal to its mark",
    "GrantAttack": "8 a point × 1.5 leverage",
    "GrantHealth": "The raw rate: an inert resource",
    "GrantMult": "Fires once and persists if the grantor dies. A version that stacks each activation is a Mk III+ scaler, not formula-priced",
    "Guard": "Priced as Taunt: different tools, each sure to do its job. Split them if the sim shows one dominating",
    "Heal": "Self-Heal is cheap because the card usually dies within 1 or 2 ticks. Passed Heal is 30% off: Biological targets are rarer and squishier",
    "Health": "Flat: no placement discount",
    "MaxAmmo": "Nearly inert alone: it needs a reload to fill",
    "MaxCharges": "Banking (spend-all dumps) and a reserve for repeated reactive triggers; spend-all scaling is unpriced upside",
    "Mult": "Each extra attack copies the attack at 8 a point, plus a surcharge (16, 40, 72, 112 for mult 2 to 5) for buff multiplication, overkill and beating Restore. Mk I Tri Gun: 1 attack, mult 3, 8 health",
    "Pierce": "Half of attack: it lands only when a card sits below the target, and never focus-fires. Revisit toward 5 to 6 a point once interiors are simulated full",
    "Recharge": "A charge is a container, priced blind to its target; a shield point is the floor. The −4 is burst leverage",
    "Reflect": "Escalates gently: Reflect never extends its own life",
    "Regen": "Above Self-Heal: Restore can bring its trigger back, and Regen fires after Restore",
    "Reload": "No surcharge: 1 ammo per volley means no burst leverage. The taper's slope is a sim knob",
    "Repair": "Passing's flexibility cancels against the support-card tax, so passed Repair costs what Self-Repair does",
    "Resist": "Resist 2 costs 64 at Mk I, so it is effectively Mk II+: it shouldn't hard-counter Mk I weapons",
    "Restore": "Above Regen: the only thing that works while the shield is down",
    "Splash": "Above attack: the rear splash nearly always lands and reaches past protectors. 10, not 12, because it doesn't focus-fire",
    "Taunt": "Rises with mark for combo headroom, not survival. Indiscriminate, so it dies faster",
    "TypeElectric": "Per hit. A 1-attack Electric gun's attack nets to 0",
    "VulnKinetic": "+1 damage per hit: about 2 hits a fight × 1 point × 8 BP",
    "armor": "**Armor** at Mk I is {armor} health with **Vulnerable (Plasma)**, which gives back {vulnOther} BP.",
    "shields": "**Shields** at Mk I is {shields} shield points with **Vulnerable (Kinetic)**, which gives back {vulnK} BP, and its free Restore 1, worth {restore}."
   }
  }
